# TASK 2 – TO-DO LIST APPLICATION

## 1. Introduction

The To-Do List Application is a simple command-line application developed using Python. The purpose of this application is to help users manage their daily tasks by providing basic operations such as adding, deleting, and viewing tasks.
The application uses a Python list to store tasks temporarily and provides a menu-driven interface through which the user can select different operations. This project was developed as part of the Python Programming Internship at CodeAlpha.

## 2. Objective

The main objectives of developing the To-Do List Application are:

* To create a simple task management application using Python.
* To allow users to add new tasks to a list.
* To allow users to delete existing tasks.
* To display all the tasks stored in the application.
* To understand the practical use of lists, loops, conditional statements, and user input in Python.
* To improve logical thinking and problem-solving skills through application development.

